  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large Dutch oven over medium heat.",
    "Add the cumin, cayenne pepper, salt, and black pepper, and cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute.",
    "Add the ginger and garlic, and cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute.",
    "Add the kimchi, and cook, stirring constantly, for 2 minutes.",
    "Add the almonds, and cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute.",
    "Add the dried apricots, and cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute.",
    "Add the pecorino cheese, and stir to combine.",
    "Transfer the mixture to a serving dish, and garnish with the parsley and cilantro.",
    "Serve immediately, and enjoy!",
    "Let the tagine rest for 10 minutes before serving, allowing the flavors to meld together.",
    "Serve the tagine with some crusty bread or over rice.",
    "Adjust the seasoning to taste, and serve hot.",
    "Garnish with additional parsley and cilantro if desired.",
    "Refrigerate any leftovers for up to 3 days."
  ],
